    <node id="Life Audit">
      <data key="d0">Life Audit</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A self-assessment practice where key life areas such as health, relationships, career, finances, mental health, and fun are rated 1–10 and analyzed for patterns, self-deception, and highest-leverage changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A life audit is a self-reflection exercise where key life domains such as health, relationships, career, and finances are rated and described honestly to identify patterns and high-leverage changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A life audit is a self-assessment method where key life areas such as health, relationships, career, and finances are rated 1–10 to identify patterns and high-leverage changes.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured self-assessment method where key life areas such as health, relationships, career, and finances are rated and described honestly to identify patterns and high-leverage changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Sabotage Analysis">
      <data key="d0">Self-Sabotage Analysis</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A reflective method where five moments of quitting, avoiding, failing, or getting stuck are described and analyzed to identify an underlying core fear, limiting belief, and hidden payoff.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Operating System">
      <data key="d0">Personal Operating System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A personalized set of 5–7 guiding principles distilled from an individual's regrets, proudest moments, hard lessons, and values, formatted as a daily personal code.&lt;SEP&gt;A personal operating system is a set of 5–7 core guiding principles distilled from regrets, proud moments, hard lessons, and non-negotiable values, used as a daily decision-making code.&lt;SEP&gt;A personal operating system is a customized set of 5–7 guiding principles derived from an individual's regrets, proud moments, and values, used as a daily decision-making code.&lt;SEP&gt;A set of 5–7 personalized guiding principles distilled from an individual's biggest regrets, proudest moments, and hard-earned lessons, intended to serve as a personal decision-making code.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hard Conversation Rehearsal">
      <data key="d0">Hard Conversation Rehearsal</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A practice of writing out a difficult situation, feelings, and fears, then using AI to clarify goals, craft constructive wording, and roleplay the other person's likely response.&lt;SEP&gt;Hard conversation rehearsal is an AI-assisted method to clarify one's real needs, phrase messages honestly without being destructive, and roleplay likely responses before engaging in a difficult conversation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Accountability System">
      <data key="d0">Accountability System</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A motivation-independent system using tiny-habit design to create small, failproof starts, with AI checking in, tracking streaks, adjusting the system, and restarting without shame after lapses.&lt;SEP&gt;An accountability system is a motivation-independent structure built on tiny habits designed to be "so small you can't fail," with consistent check-ins, streak tracking, and shame-free restarts.&lt;SEP&gt;An accountability system is a motivation-proof structure designed to maintain habits through small achievable starts, check-ins, streak tracking, and shame-free restarts.&lt;SEP&gt;A structured system designed to track habits and streaks, check in with specific questions, adjust the system rather than the goal, and allow shame-free resets after lapses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emotional Trigger Decoding">
      <data key="d0">Emotional Trigger Decoding</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A real-time emotional processing practice where one describes what happened, names emotions, rates intensity, and uses AI-guided questioning to trace reactions to deeper roots such as past patterns, unmet needs, and original wounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Emotional trigger decoding is a step-by-step AI-assisted process to trace intense emotional reactions to their deeper sources, such as unmet needs or earlier experiences, framed as therapy-adjacent reflection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Letter Writing Exercise">
      <data key="d0">Letter Writing Exercise</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An expressive writing technique used to process unresolved relationships or unfinished emotional business, with AI reflecting back core emotions and unmet needs to help craft a final version for personal closure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AI">
      <data key="d0">AI</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An accessible conversational tool used as a nightly or morning instrument to facilitate structured self-reflection, pattern recognition, and personal development across multiple life domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence used as a nonjudgmental external thinking partner to support self-awareness, personal growth, reflection, and structured self-conversation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122031</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BJ Fogg">
      <data key="d0">BJ Fogg</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">BJ Fogg is referenced as the creator of tiny-habit design, a behavioral methodology that makes habit starts so small they are nearly impossible to fail.&lt;SEP&gt;BJ Fogg is referenced as the originator of the "so small you can't fail" habit-building approach, cited in the context of designing effective accountability systems.&lt;SEP&gt;BJ Fogg is referenced in the context of tiny habits, a behavioral design approach where habits are made so small they cannot fail.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher associated with the "tiny habits" approach, which involves designing habits so small that failure is nearly impossible, referenced in the context of motivation-proof accountability systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tiny-Habit Design">
      <data key="d0">Tiny-Habit Design</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A behavioral design framework attributed to BJ Fogg that makes the start of a habit so small it cannot be failed, used as a foundation for building reliable accountability systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dopamine">
      <data key="d0">Dopamine</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dopamine is described as a neurochemical associated with anticipation rather than reward, used to explain why motivation is considered unreliable as a basis for habit formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Dopamine is described as the neurochemical driving motivation through anticipation, which fades after planning, explaining why willpower alone is insufficient for habit maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;A neurotransmitter tied to anticipation rather than sustained motivation, cited as the reason motivation is unreliable and accountability systems are needed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mindless Consumption">
      <data key="d0">Mindless Consumption</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The practice of scrolling others' opinions without intentional engagement, contrasted with structured self-reflection as a less productive use of time and attention.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Structured Self-Conversation">
      <data key="d0">Structured Self-Conversation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A practice of spending intentional time, as little as 10 minutes, in reflective dialogue to regain clarity, spot patterns, and build momentum in life, facilitated by AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prompt Framework">
      <data key="d0">Prompt Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A structured set of instructions or templates used to guide AI interactions for specific self-reflection and personal development purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Expressive Writing">
      <data key="d0">Expressive Writing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Expressive writing is an uncensored writing exercise directed at someone or oneself to unload unresolved feelings, aided by AI to identify core emotions and craft a final honest letter for closure.&lt;SEP&gt;A writing technique used to process unresolved emotional experiences and relationships, forming the basis of the Letter Writing Exercise.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique involving writing to unload unresolved emotions, used in the "letter you'll never send" exercise to achieve emotional closure by reflecting core emotions and unmet needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Expressive writing is the practice of writing unfiltered, uncensored thoughts and emotions as a way to process and release unresolved feelings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Original Wound">
      <data key="d0">Original Wound</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A foundational emotional injury from the past that underlies present-day emotional triggers and reactions, identified through the Emotional Trigger Decoding method.&lt;SEP&gt;The original wound refers to the deeper emotional source or earlier experience to which intense emotional reactions can be traced during emotional trigger decoding.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Core Fear">
      <data key="d0">Core Fear</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep-seated fear identified through Self-Sabotage Analysis as an underlying driver of self-defeating behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Limiting Belief">
      <data key="d0">Limiting Belief</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A restrictive belief identified through Self-Sabotage Analysis that contributes to patterns of self-sabotage and avoidance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c19ebc4badbd8262c8487882ac0285a9</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ChatGPT">
      <data key="d0">ChatGPT</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">ChatGPT is an AI tool described as an "externalized thinking partner" that helps users gain self-awareness, identify patterns, and reflect more honestly on their lives.&lt;SEP&gt;ChatGPT is an AI tool discussed in the video as a powerful means for self-awareness, personal growth, and structured self-reflection rather than just productivity.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI tool referenced as an example of AI technology that can be used for self-awareness and personal development rather than just productivity tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Claude">
      <data key="d0">Claude</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Claude is an AI tool mentioned alongside ChatGPT as an example of AI systems that can serve as nonjudgmental external thinking partners for personal growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude is an AI assistant/model used for building AI apps, capable of reading/writing files, running shell commands, and connecting to external systems via APIs and MCP.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude is an AI model developed by Anthropic, available in variants including Haiku, Sonnet, and Opus, used for tasks ranging from simple queries to complex reasoning.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude is an AI assistant (also referred to as Claude Code) that can perform tasks such as reading/writing files, running shell commands, and generating responses based on prompts.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude is an AI system (Claude Code) that can access files, create/edit files, run shell commands, and perform complex AI-assisted tasks for users.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude is an AI system developed for coding and general assistance, capable of searching data, answering questions, editing files, running shell commands, and cooperating with sub-agents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Awareness">
      <data key="d0">Self-Awareness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-awareness is described as the biggest predictor of success across relationships, career, health, and well-being, with research suggesting only 10–15% of people are truly self-aware.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-awareness is described as the most powerful use of AI, contrasted with productivity, and noted as rare among people due to biased self-perception.&lt;SEP&gt;A skill strongly linked to success and well-being; research suggests only 10–15% of people are genuinely self-aware, often hindered by the introspection illusion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Introspection Illusion">
      <data key="d0">Introspection Illusion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The introspection illusion is a cognitive bias where people believe they are self-aware but often cannot accurately perceive their own patterns and blind spots.&lt;SEP&gt;The introspection illusion is the concept that the human mind struggles to evaluate itself accurately, leading to biased self-reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;A cognitive bias where humans, when looking inward, tend to protect their self-image and rationalize rather than perceiving themselves clearly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cognitive Dissonance">
      <data key="d0">Cognitive Dissonance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cognitive dissonance is the tendency to avoid discomfort, which leads people to shy away from honest self-reflection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Sabotage">
      <data key="d0">Self-Sabotage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-sabotage refers to recurring behaviors such as quitting, avoiding, or getting stuck, analyzed as symptoms of deeper core fears, limiting beliefs, and hidden payoffs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hidden Payoff">
      <data key="d0">Hidden Payoff</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The hidden payoff is the psychological protection provided by self-sabotaging patterns, often shielding individuals from judgment or evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;The hidden payoff is the unconscious benefit or protection that a self-sabotage pattern provides to an individual, shielding them from deeper fears or discomfort.&lt;SEP&gt;The underlying benefit or protection that a self-sabotage pattern provides to an individual, shielding them from a perceived deeper fear or threat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122032</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Psychological Distance">
      <data key="d0">Psychological Distance</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Psychological distance is the mental clarity and emotional regulation gained by externalizing and writing down thoughts, which helps individuals evaluate their situations more objectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Psychological distance is the mental separation AI creates between a person and their thoughts, helping them observe patterns and blind spots more objectively.&lt;SEP&gt;A cognitive state created by externalizing thoughts into structured dialogue, which improves clarity and emotional regulation by separating the individual from their immediate emotional experience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Therapy is a professional mental health practice that AI tools like ChatGPT are explicitly noted not to replace, despite their utility in self-reflection.&lt;SEP&gt;Professional mental health support that AI is explicitly noted should not replace, though AI can meaningfully support reflection alongside it.&lt;SEP&gt;Therapy is professional mental health support, explicitly noted in the video as something AI cannot and should not replace, though AI can serve as a therapy-adjacent reflection tool.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Relationships">
      <data key="d0">Human Relationships</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal connections between people that AI is explicitly noted should not replace, though AI can support and improve real-life conversations and decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Human relationships are real-world interpersonal connections that AI is explicitly noted as unable to replace, but can help individuals show up better within.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c69eb46b9fdf4cfbf2d4e228fde1a76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
