      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Sabotage Pattern">
      <data key="d0">Self-Sabotage Pattern</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-sabotage patterns are recurring behaviors such as quitting, avoiding, or procrastinating, which share an underlying fear, belief, or hidden payoff that protects the individual from something.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unsent Letter">
      <data key="d0">Unsent Letter</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An unsent letter is an unfiltered expressive writing exercise addressed to another person or one's past self, used to release unresolved emotions and identify unmet needs.&lt;SEP&gt;A writing exercise in which unspoken anger, grief, or love toward someone or one's past self is expressed, with AI helping reflect unmet needs and produce a final unfiltered version aimed at emotional closure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emotional Trigger">
      <data key="d0">Emotional Trigger</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An emotional trigger is a disproportionate emotional reaction to a surface event that points to a deeper underlying wound or unmet need.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Difficult Conversation Rehearsal">
      <data key="d0">Difficult Conversation Rehearsal</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Difficult conversation rehearsal is a practice method where an individual clarifies their needs, crafts honest language, and roleplays the other person's likely responses before having a real conversation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tiny Habits">
      <data key="d0">Tiny Habits</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Tiny habits is a behavioral approach associated with BJ Fogg, where habit starts are made extremely small to ensure consistent success without reliance on motivation.&lt;SEP&gt;A habit-formation approach, associated with BJ Fogg, that involves creating starter habits so small they cannot be failed, used to build accountability systems that do not rely on motivation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Connection">
      <data key="d0">Human Connection</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human connection is emphasized as something that AI tools like ChatGPT should not replace, even while being used to deepen self-reflection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3cdd347d2c888fa651c16760dc54aac4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Sabotage Patterns">
      <data key="d0">Self-Sabotage Patterns</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Recurring behaviors such as quitting, avoiding, or getting stuck, which are analyzed to uncover deeper fears, core beliefs, and hidden payoffs that protect the individual from perceived threats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emotional Triggers">
      <data key="d0">Emotional Triggers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reactions involving being overreactive or emotionally flooded, which can be traced through step-by-step questioning to deeper sources, old wounds, or recurring patterns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pattern Recognition">
      <data key="d0">Pattern Recognition</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A capability of AI that makes it especially useful for identifying recurring behaviors, self-deception, and emotional patterns across multiple data points shared by the user.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TikTok Video Script">
      <data key="d0">TikTok Video Script</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A video script format summarizing seven practical ways to use AI for personal growth, emphasizing self-awareness and structured self-conversation over productivity tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="YouTube Shorts Script">
      <data key="d0">YouTube Shorts Script</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A video script format summarizing how AI can function as an externalized thinking partner for self-awareness, covering seven practical uses with prompt frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb01cd2d607a14da2729a2994a8833a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122033</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Difficult Conversations">
      <data key="d0">Difficult Conversations</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A practical technique involving clarifying what one needs from a conversation, crafting honest-but-non-destructive wording, and roleplaying the other person's likely responses to prepare for challenging interpersonal exchanges.</data>
