    <node id="Claude Code">
      <data key="d0">Claude Code</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Claude Code is an AI-powered coding tool developed by Anthropic, featuring concepts such as tools, permission modes, context windows, and sub-agents for software development tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude Code is a tool or framework built around Claude that enables developers and non-technical users to build, connect systems, and use power features like sub-agents and checkpoints.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)">
      <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RAG is a method where Claude searches user-provided data and answers based on that source, enabling more accurate and contextually grounded responses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sub-Agents">
      <data key="d0">Sub-Agents</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sub-agents are specialized AI helpers that cooperate on different tasks, functioning like multiple agents in an AI "agency."&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-agents are multiple specialized AI agents that work together, like an AI agency, to split and handle complex tasks collaboratively.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-agents are multiple specialized AI helpers that coordinate to divide and handle complex workflows, functioning like an AI agency.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-agents are multiple specialized AI helpers that cooperate within an AI agency framework to complete complex tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Checkpoints And Undo">
      <data key="d0">Checkpoints And Undo</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Checkpoints and Undo is a Claude feature that auto-saves project states and allows users to revert edits, providing safety when Claude modifies files.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkpoints and undo is a feature in Claude that auto-saves changes and allows users to revert to previous versions.&lt;SEP&gt;A feature in Claude Code that automatically saves progress and allows users to revert changes, providing a safety net during development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Plan Mode">
      <data key="d0">Plan Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Plan mode is a safe permissions mode in which Claude proposes changes before executing them, recommended for learning or working on live projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Plan mode is a permission mode in Claude Code recommended for safety, where Claude plans actions before executing them.&lt;SEP&gt;Plan mode is a permissions mode in Claude that is considered the safest option for working on live or sensitive projects, requiring approval before making changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Plan mode is a permission mode in Claude that generates a plan without changing code, recommended for live or important projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Plan mode is a safe permission setting in Claude where no edits are made, allowing users to review planned actions before execution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bypass Permission">
      <data key="d0">Bypass Permission</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Bypass permission is a command that allows Claude to skip repeated permission prompts and automatically make edits, recommended only when the user trusts Claude and has backups.&lt;SEP&gt;Bypass permission (dangerous_skip_permission) is a mode that speeds up workflows by skipping permission prompts, but requires caution and is recommended only when backups or undo are available.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Claude.md">
      <data key="d0">Claude.md</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Claude.md is a project-specific long-term memory file (MD format) created using the /init command to store persistent project information and avoid repeating context.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude.md is a file created with the /init command that stores long-term project memory and persistent context for Claude Code projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude.md is a markdown file created via /init that serves as a project's long-term memory, preserving context across sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Claude.md is a project long-term memory file created via the /init command, recommended for every repository to maintain persistent project context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
