    <node id="API">
      <data key="d0">API</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An API (Application Programming Interface) is a key that allows apps to communicate with each other, providing limited and controlled access.&lt;SEP&gt;An API (Application Programming Interface) is a key that grants limited, controlled access to an application or service.&lt;SEP&gt;An API (Application Programming Interface) is a key or interface that allows external applications and services to communicate with each other, such as the Notion API.&lt;SEP&gt;An API is a key used to access specific functionality of an application, likened to a door key.&lt;SEP&gt;An API is a key used to access specific application features, described as providing limited access points to app functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Context Window">
      <data key="d0">Context Window</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The context window is Claude's short-term chat memory with an input/output token limit; it can fill up during long conversations, supporting up to approximately 1 million tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;The context window refers to the short-term chat history available to Claude during a session, with a capacity cited as up to 1 million tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;The context window is the model's short-term memory, consisting of chat history, and has a finite size limit.&lt;SEP&gt;The context window is Claude's short-term memory for the current chat session, with an input/output token limit.&lt;SEP&gt;The context window is Claude's short-term memory for a chat session, which has a size limit and can be managed by compacting conversation history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tokens">
      <data key="d0">Tokens</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tokens are the measurement unit for Claude's usage and cost, roughly corresponding to units of text or words processed.&lt;SEP&gt;Tokens are the unit of usage and cost for Claude, roughly equivalent to one word each; Claude charges by tokens, making usage monitoring important.&lt;SEP&gt;Tokens are the unit of text processing in Claude, roughly equivalent to one word each, and their usage incurs costs that scale with plan size.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prompt Engineering">
      <data key="d0">Prompt Engineering</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Prompt engineering is the practice of crafting clearer and more specific instructions for Claude, including assigning roles to improve output quality.&lt;SEP&gt;Prompt engineering is the practice of writing clearer, role-based natural-language instructions to obtain better results from AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Prompt engineering is the practice of writing clearer, role-based prompts to obtain better AI results, such as instructing the AI to "act as a senior web developer."&lt;SEP&gt;Prompt engineering is the practice of crafting clearer, role-based, and specific prompts to achieve better results from Claude.&lt;SEP&gt;Prompt engineering is the practice of writing clearer, role-based instructions to obtain better results from AI models like Claude.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122165</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="JSON">
      <data key="d0">JSON</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">JSON is a structured data format used by computers to organize information, which Claude can generate and format on behalf of users.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON is a structured data format used by computers to organize and exchange information, which Claude can generate and organize.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON is a structured data format used for organizing information, preferred by computers for data exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON is a structured data format used to organize information, preferred by computers for data exchange.&lt;SEP&gt;JSON is a structured data format used by computers, referenced in the context of data exchange with Claude and connected systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
