    </node>
    <node id="Git">
      <data key="d0">Git</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Git is a version control system that tracks changes in code files, allowing users to revert to earlier versions.&lt;SEP&gt;Git is a version control system that tracks changes and manages versioning of code and files in a project.&lt;SEP&gt;Git is a version control system that tracks changes to files and allows users to revert to earlier versions, functioning like an autosave or history system.&lt;SEP&gt;Git is a version control system that tracks changes to files, allowing users to revert to earlier versions.&lt;SEP&gt;Git is a version control system that tracks changes to code, allowing users to revert to previous states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
