    <node id="Front End">
      <data key="d0">Front End</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Front end refers to the user-facing part of a web application, representing what users see and interact with directly.&lt;SEP&gt;Front end refers to the part of a system that users see and interact with directly.&lt;SEP&gt;Front end refers to the user interface layer of an application, contrasted with back-end server and data logic.&lt;SEP&gt;Front end refers to the part of an application that users see and interact with directly.&lt;SEP&gt;The front end refers to the part of an application that users see and interact with, exemplified by platforms like Vercel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Back End">
      <data key="d0">Back End</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Back end refers to the server, data, and logic layer of a web application, operating behind the scenes.&lt;SEP&gt;Back end refers to the underlying internal logic and data systems of an application.&lt;SEP&gt;Back end refers to the server and data logic layer of an application, contrasted with the front-end user interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Back end refers to the underlying functionality and data processing of an application, not visible to users.&lt;SEP&gt;The back end refers to the part of an application that runs behind the scenes, exemplified by platforms like Supabase.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-025a86a4903e4e489cd42bedaffcb840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122166</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MCP (Model Context Protocol)">
      <data key="d0">MCP (Model Context Protocol)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">MCP is described as a "master key" that allows Claude deeper and broader access to apps, enabling it to act on the user's behalf inside applications.&lt;SEP&gt;MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a protocol described as a powerful "master key" that allows AI models to act across an application on a user's behalf, enabling edits and changes.&lt;SEP&gt;MCP is described as a "master key" that gives Claude broader in-app control, enabling it to act on a user's behalf inside an application.&lt;SEP&gt;MCP is described as a "master key" that provides broader access, allowing Claude to act on a user's behalf inside an application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1694023022122e91d5653a390a57c8f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)">
      <data key="d0">RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">RAG is a method where Claude answers queries by retrieving and using data from user-provided documents or databases for more accurate responses.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) is a method where Claude uses provided data from documents or databases to answer questions, improving accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG is a method where Claude retrieves information from user-supplied data to accurately answer questions, generating responses grounded in that content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ab74c3d2ad783400aacdc12951dd5004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b97dc56900235cb8d228fef7c8405c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-047f3904283ca1416cabe7cde1e03247</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1774122167</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
