    <edge source="Front End" target="Back End">
      <data key="d7">2.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Front end and back end represent the two complementary layers of an application: the user-facing interface and the underlying data/functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Front end and back end represent the two complementary layers of application architecture, distinguishing what users see from what runs behind the scenes.</data>
      <data key="d9">application architecture,architecture,contrast,separation of concerns</data>
